EXT. SHELL CRATER, NO MAN'S LAND - DAWN

Mud. Barbed wire. A dead tree.

Five soldiers crouch in the crater. SERGEANT BELL, 40s. CORPORAL NIKOS, 20s. PRIVATE HARGROVE, 18. PRIVATE SANDOVAL, 30s. And a man in a different uniform, face down in the mud, with a bandaged shoulder: a PRISONER.

Nikos shakes the Prisoner awake.

BELL
Name?

PRISONER
Anders.

BELL
Rank?

PRISONER
Nothing. I carried the bread.

Hargrove laughs. Sandoval shushes him. Shells whistle overhead.

NIKOS
Sarge, he's lying.

BELL
He's hungry.

Bell tosses him a hardtack. The Prisoner eats.

HARGROVE
He's our enemy, Sarge.

BELL
Anders is his name.

ANDERS
Thank you.

A whistle. Everyone ducks. The shell lands thirty yards away. Mud rains down. Anders crawls toward Hargrove and covers the boy's helmet with both hands.

SANDOVAL
(to Bell)
Sarge, he saved the kid.

BELL
Anders. Stay close.
